      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Rye’s economy has long hinged on cattle ranching and dryland farming, the mainstay of its rural character.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://colorado.wiki/a/Rye,_Colorado",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Rye enjoys a rare subtropical highland climate, where mountain rainstorms give it more precipitation than typical semi‑arid Colorado towns.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15,
        16,
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rye%2C_Colorado",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Today, Rye attracts residents who crave quiet life and easy access to nearby Greenhorn Mountain Wilderness and San Isabel National Forest.",
